     --qq      Include active queue statistics.  Each priority queue has both
             pending (ppeenndd) and active (aaccttiivv) I/O requests.  Pending requests
             are waiting to be issued to the disk, and active requests have
             been issued to disk and are waiting for completion.  These stats
             are broken out by priority queue:
             ssyynnccqq__rreeaadd//wwrriittee   Current number of entries in synchronous pri‐
                                ority queues.
             aassyynnccqq__rreeaadd//wwrriittee  Current number of entries in asynchronous pri‐
                                ority queues.
             ssccrruubbqq__rreeaadd        Current number of entries in scrub queue.
             ttrriimmqq__wwrriittee        Current number of entries in trim queue.
             rreebbuuiillddqq__wwrriittee     Current number of entries in rebuild queue.

             All queue statistics are instantaneous measurements of the number
             of entries in the queues.  If you specify an interval, the mea‐
             surements will be sampled from the end of the interval.

