   EExxaammppllee 1133: Adding Cache Devices to a ZFS Pool
     The following command adds two disks for use as cache devices to a ZFS
     storage pool:
           # zzppooooll aadddd _p_o_o_l ccaacchhee _s_d_c _s_d_d

     Once added, the cache devices gradually fill with content from main mem‐
     ory.  Depending on the size of your cache devices, it could take over an
     hour for them to fill.  Capacity and reads can be monitored using the
     iioossttaatt subcommand as follows:
           # zzppooooll iioossttaatt --vv _p_o_o_l _5

